mapping "XAH.99.ZZ.1" source="XAH.99.ZZ" target="SNOMED_CT:129267009" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source XAH.99.ZZ SNOMED CT 129267009 = a residual Swedish social-service code for administrative
        activity spanning multiple process steps (other specified and unspecified) — a catch-all
        administrative/case-handling category. Target (sv synonym) is the generic administrative-action
        concept. Why this target: exact Swedish-synonym match and the only standard concept carrying
        generic semantics. Why related (not broader/exact): the SNOMED CT concept is a generic
        international healthcare-administration term, whereas the source is a Swedish social-services
        multi-step case-handling residual; the association is real (both denote non-clinical
        administrative activity) but the source's social-services/statute frame and residual-bucket
        nature make only a loose link defensible — per §related, capped at. Athena-local (synonyms.tdl);
        no web.
        """
}
mapping "YAA.1" source="YAA" target="SNOMED_CT:183425000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source YAA SNOMED CT 183425000 = the top-level category for social-services interventions for
        elderly persons and persons with disability under the Swedish Social Services Act (SoL) — a
        two-population parent category spanning all SoL support measures. Target (regime/therapy, sv) is
        the OMOP standard concept for social-care regimes broadly. Why this target: closest standard
        concept for the social-care-intervention axis; no SoL-anchored standard concept exists. Why
        broader: substantial breadth mismatch — SNOMED CT social care covers all social-care regimes (all
        ages, all statutes, all populations) whereas the source is the elder/disabled SoL category; per
        §1 low tier. Consistent with peer YAC/YAB.05 parent-category handling. Athena-local; no web.
        """
}
